  "details": "On the VRChat Ask Forum, when a post is flagged for moderation, its contents are temporarily hidden. However, the post contents are not hidden in HTML source view from `<meta property=\"og:description\">` and `<meta name=\"twitter:description\">` when this happens.\n\nWhen a temporarily hidden post is then shared to instant messaging software or shared on social media, the full post will be seen.\n\nSteps to reproduce:\n\n1. Post something on the VRChat Ask forums.\n\n2. On another account, flag the post for moderation review for a reason (e.g., inappropriateness). The post will become temporarily hidden for everyone.\n\n3. On any non-moderator account or as a guest visitor, click the post date for the URL pointing to that temporarily hidden post, then share the URL or view the HTML source of that URL.\n\nAffected URL: https://ask.vrchat.com/t/ai-vrchat-worlds/49088/16\n\nExpected result: Temporarily hiding the post should also hide the post from meta tags.\n\nActual result: Flagged content is temporarily hidden in body, but not in HTML source or when shared on instant messaging apps/social media, defeating the purpose of temporarily hiding posts.",
